  "ruleTraffic01Title": "Highway & Arterial Speed Limits",
  "ruleTraffic01Summary": "Maximum speed limit of 100 km/h on expressways and a minimum of 60 km/h.",
  "ruleTraffic01Penalty": "Maximum fine of Rp 500,000 or up to 2 months imprisonment",
  "ruleTraffic01Explanation": "Drivers must obey posted speed limit signs. On intercity toll roads, the speed range is 60 to 100 km/h. On inner-city toll roads, the limit is 80 km/h. Intercity roads allow up to 80 km/h, urban zones 50 km/h, and residential zones 30 km/h.",
  "ruleTraffic01Dos": "Pay close attention to speed signs along every stretch\nKeep a safe following distance using the 3-second rule",
  "ruleTraffic01Donts": "Drive over 100 km/h on toll roads\nDrive slowly in the far-right passing lane",
  "ruleTraffic02Title": "Prohibition of Phone Use While Driving",
  "ruleTraffic02Summary": "Operating mobile devices or engaging in distracting activities while driving is strictly prohibited.",
  "ruleTraffic02Penalty": "Maximum fine of Rp 750,000 or up to 3 months imprisonment",
  "ruleTraffic02Explanation": "Drivers are prohibited from any activity that disrupts concentration, including texting, watching video content, or holding a phone while operating a moving vehicle.",
  "ruleTraffic02Dos": "Mount your phone on a dashboard holder and set navigation beforehand\nPull over in a safe parking zone before taking emergency calls",
  "ruleTraffic02Donts": "Reply to chats or scroll social feeds while waiting at traffic lights\nHold a phone to your ear while steering",
  "ruleTraffic03Title": "Mandatory Driver License & Vehicle Registration",
  "ruleTraffic03Summary": "Drivers must hold a valid driver license and present official vehicle registration upon inspection.",
  "ruleTraffic03Penalty": "No license: max Rp 1,000,000 fine; No registration card: max Rp 500,000 fine",
  "ruleTraffic03Explanation": "Every motorist on public roads must hold a valid license matching the vehicle class and carry the authentic vehicle registration certificate (STNK).",
  "ruleTraffic03Dos": "Check license expiration and annual road tax validation regularly\nCarry original cards or official verified digital credentials",
  "ruleTraffic03Donts": "Drive without holding an active, valid license\nLend vehicles to underage or unlicensed individuals",
  "ruleTraffic04Title": "Motorcycle Daytime Running Headlights (DRL)",
  "ruleTraffic04Summary": "Motorcycle riders must keep low-beam headlights on during day and night hours.",
  "ruleTraffic04Penalty": "Maximum fine of Rp 100,000 or up to 15 days detention",
  "ruleTraffic04Explanation": "To maximize vehicle visibility and avoid severe collisions, two-wheeled motor vehicles must operate daytime running headlights continuously.",
  "ruleTraffic04Dos": "Ensure low-beam headlights turn on automatically with ignition\nReplace damaged bulbs immediately",
  "ruleTraffic04Donts": "Install hidden kill-switches to shut off daytime lights\nMount illegal blinding strobe or high-intensity spotlights",
  "ruleTraffic05Title": "Certified Safety Helmet Requirement (SNI)",
  "ruleTraffic05Summary": "Motorcycle drivers and passengers must wear helmets certified under Indonesian National Standards (SNI).",
  "ruleTraffic05Penalty": "Maximum fine of Rp 250,000 or up to 1 month detention",
  "ruleTraffic05Explanation": "Riders and passengers must wear an SNI-certified helmet with the chin strap fastened securely until it clicks before riding on public streets.",
  "ruleTraffic05Dos": "Verify the embossed SNI mark on the helmet shell\nFasten chin straps firmly until they click into locked position",
  "ruleTraffic05Donts": "Use construction hard hats or bicycle helmets for motorcycling\nLeave helmet chin straps unbuckled or dangling",
  "ruleTraffic06Title": "Prohibition Against Driving Counter-Traffic",
  "ruleTraffic06Summary": "Driving against designated traffic flow or one-way street signage is strictly forbidden.",
  "ruleTraffic06Penalty": "Maximum fine of Rp 500,000 or up to 2 months imprisonment",
  "ruleTraffic06Explanation": "Driving against traffic creates extreme hazards for all road users and remains one of the top causes of fatal traffic accidents.",
  "ruleTraffic06Dos": "Follow one-way road signs and directional arrows strictly\nUse official U-turn locations even if further away",
  "ruleTraffic06Donts": "Ride against oncoming traffic in alleys, sidewalks, or flyovers\nFollow reckless motorists attempting shortcuts against traffic",
  "ruleTraffic07Title": "Prohibition of Vehicles in Dedicated Busway Lanes",
  "ruleTraffic07Summary": "Private vehicles are forbidden from entering or driving along dedicated public transit busways.",
  "ruleTraffic07Penalty": "Maximum fine of Rp 500,000 or up to 2 months imprisonment",
  "ruleTraffic07Explanation": "Busway lanes are strictly sterile corridors reserved exclusively for transit buses and legally authorized emergency units (ambulances, fire trucks).",
  "ruleTraffic07Dos": "Stay inside regular traffic lanes even in heavy traffic\nYield when transit buses maneuver through intersections",
  "ruleTraffic07Donts": "Cross into busways to bypass congested lanes\nStop or park near busway lane gates and barriers",
  "ruleTraffic08Title": "Exhaust Noise Limits & Roadworthiness Standards",
  "ruleTraffic08Summary": "Motor vehicles must comply with legal acoustic noise thresholds and technical roadworthiness.",
  "ruleTraffic08Penalty": "Maximum fine of Rp 250,000 or up to 1 month detention",
  "ruleTraffic08Explanation": "Unmuffled racing exhausts violate statutory decibel noise limits established by environmental regulations and vehicle roadworthiness standards.",
  "ruleTraffic08Dos": "Use factory-standard exhausts or certified street-legal mufflers\nConduct regular emissions testing and scheduled maintenance",
  "ruleTraffic08Donts": "Install loud open straight-pipe exhausts in residential areas\nRemove side mirrors or blinkers for racing appearance",
  "ruleLabor01Title": "Working Hours & Overtime Wage Calculation",
  "ruleLabor01Summary": "Maximum 40 hours per week. Overtime capped at 4 hours/day and 18 hours/week with statutory overtime pay.",
  "ruleLabor01Penalty": "Overtime pay is a mandatory employee entitlement; penal fines apply to non-compliant employers",
  "ruleLabor01Explanation": "Standard working hours are 7 hours/day (6-day week) or 8 hours/day (5-day week). Overtime requires written employee agreement. Compensation is 1.5x hourly wage for the first hour and 2x for subsequent hours.",
  "ruleLabor01Dos": "Maintain personal records of actual overtime clock-in and clock-out times\nEnsure an official written overtime instruction exists from your manager",
  "ruleLabor01Donts": "Work overtime beyond statutory limits of 4 hours daily or 18 hours weekly\nAccept unpaid overtime arrangements lacking formal statutory compensation",
  "ruleLabor02Title": "Annual Leave & Statutory Paid Time Off",
  "ruleLabor02Summary": "Workers are entitled to at least 12 working days of paid annual leave after 12 consecutive months of service.",
  "ruleLabor02Penalty": "Absolute employee entitlement with full wages; administrative sanctions and fines apply to violating employers",
  "ruleLabor02Explanation": "Employers must grant at least 12 working days of annual leave with full wages to staff with 12 months continuous service. Maternity leave provides 1.5 months before and 1.5 months after delivery.",
  "ruleLabor02Dos": "Submit annual leave plans according to official company procedures\nRetain written approval records and verified remaining balance statements",
  "ruleLabor02Donts": "Deduct basic wages for taking statutory paid leave entitlements\nForfeit unused leave balances without documented compensation arrangements",
  "ruleLabor03Title": "Religious Holiday Allowance (THR)",
  "ruleLabor03Summary": "Religious Holiday Allowance must be paid in full at least 7 days (H-7) prior to the religious celebration.",
  "ruleLabor03Penalty": "Late payment penalty of 5% of total unpaid THR plus formal administrative sanctions",
  "ruleLabor03Explanation": "Employers must pay THR to staff with at least 1 month continuous tenure. Staff with 12+ months service receive 1 month wages; under 12 months receive prorated pay: (months worked / 12) x 1 month wage.",
  "ruleLabor03Dos": "Note the statutory H-7 deadline ahead of your religious holiday\nFile reports with the Ministry of Manpower THR hotline if pay is overdue or installment-based",
  "ruleLabor03Donts": "Accept food hampers or goods as a substitute for cash THR payments\nAccept THR installments without formal labor office mediation and written consent",
  "ruleLabor04Title": "Termination Compensation (Severance & Service Pay)",
  "ruleLabor04Summary": "Companies must pay statutory Severance, Long Service Recognition, and Compensation of Rights based on tenure and cause.",
  "ruleLabor04Penalty": "Full compensation is mandatory; legally enforceable through Industrial Court and labor inspectorates",
  "ruleLabor04Explanation": "Upon layoffs, employers must pay Severance Pay (up to 9 months wages), Long Service Pay / UPMK (up to 10 months wages), and Compensation of Rights / UPH (unused leave/relocation). Multipliers apply depending on the formal layoff rationale.",
  "ruleLabor04Dos": "Demand formal written statements of the official termination grounds\nUse statutory severance calculators to verify exact entitlement numbers before signing documents",
  "ruleLabor04Donts": "Sign coerced or fabricated resignation letters that extinguish severance rights\nAccept severance settlements falling below statutory minimums under Government Regulation 35/2021",
  "ruleLabor05Title": "Fixed-Term Contract End Compensation (PKWT)",
  "ruleLabor05Summary": "Fixed-term contract workers are entitled to compensation money upon the expiration or renewal of their contract term.",
  "ruleLabor05Penalty": "Compensation must be disbursed no later than the final day of the contractual term",
  "ruleLabor05Explanation": "Employers must pay compensation to fixed-term employees with at least 1 month of service whenever a contract finishes or renews. Formula: (Months of Service / 12) x 1 month wage.",
  "ruleLabor05Dos": "Confirm that the contract clearly states precise start and end dates\nCalculate and settle PKWT compensation at each contract completion before extension",
  "ruleLabor05Donts": "Assume contract workers hold no statutory compensation rights\nKeep employees on rolling temporary contracts indefinitely for permanent core jobs",
  "ruleLabor06Title": "Mandatory Social Security Enrollment (BPJS Ketenagakerjaan)",
  "ruleLabor06Summary": "Employers must enroll all staff in BPJS Employment programs covering accident, death, old age, and pension insurance.",
  "ruleLabor06Penalty": "Denial of commercial public licensing and administrative late fee penalties for non-compliant employers",
  "ruleLabor06Explanation": "Employers are legally mandated to register employees into Work Accident (JKK), Death (JKM), Old-Age (JHT), and Pension (JP) schemes and regularly remit their monthly contributions.",
  "ruleLabor06Dos": "Verify active membership and check old-age savings balances via the official JMO app\nReport to labor authorities if employee salary deductions are not forwarded to BPJS",
  "ruleLabor06Donts": "Permit payroll wage deductions without receiving genuine official BPJS participant cards\nEngage in hazardous tasks without verified Work Accident Insurance coverage",
  "rulePrivacy01Title": "Online Defamation & Cyber Complaint Offenses",
  "rulePrivacy01Summary": "Attacking reputation online is an absolute complaint offense; public interest criticism is exempt from criminal liability.",
  "rulePrivacy01Penalty": "Maximum 2 years imprisonment and/or a maximum fine of Rp 400,000,000",
  "rulePrivacy01Explanation": "The 2024 ITE Law Revision affirms that online defamation is an absolute complaint offense that can only be prosecuted upon direct complaint by individual victims. Legitimate public interest critique and lawful self-defense are strictly non-punishable.",
  "rulePrivacy01Dos": "Base public commentary on verifiable facts, documented data, and credible sources\nUse polite, professional phrasing without personal insults or profanity",
  "rulePrivacy01Donts": "Disseminate unsubstantiated scandalous accusations or slander on public feeds\nCreate impersonating accounts to spread false rumors and gossip",
  "rulePrivacy02Title": "Personal Data Subject Rights (PDP Law)",
  "rulePrivacy02Summary": "Individuals have the legal right to access, rectify, erase, and revoke consent for their personal data.",
  "rulePrivacy02Penalty": "Administrative fines up to 2% of annual corporate turnover for non-compliant data controllers",
  "rulePrivacy02Explanation": "The Personal Data Protection Law guarantees individual rights to request data records, rectify inaccuracies, restrict processing, and seek damages for unlawful data breaches committed by corporate or public agencies.",
  "rulePrivacy02Dos": "Submit formal account deletion requests when closing digital platform accounts\nAudit app permissions on smartphones for contacts, microphone, and location",
  "rulePrivacy02Donts": "Share uncensored ID cards, family registries, or bank accounts in open messaging groups\nAccept terms for apps demanding permissions unrelated to core product functions",
  "rulePrivacy03Title": "Data Breach Notification Duty (72-Hour Rule)",
  "rulePrivacy03Summary": "Data controllers must issue written notification of data breaches within 72 hours of discovery.",
  "rulePrivacy03Penalty": "Written warnings, business operation freezes, and substantial statutory administrative fines",
  "rulePrivacy03Explanation": "Upon any security breach or data compromise, the data controller must notify affected data subjects and the regulatory commission in writing within 72 hours, explaining the incident and containment steps.",
  "rulePrivacy03Dos": "Immediately reset passwords and enable app-based 2FA upon receiving a breach alert\nMonitor bank statements and unexpected multi-factor login alerts closely",
  "rulePrivacy03Donts": "Conceal system intrusions from public users and supervisory regulators\nIgnore verified security incident notifications sent by reputable service providers",
  "rulePrivacy04Title": "Prohibition Against Unauthorized Doxxing",
  "rulePrivacy04Summary": "Publishing or distributing another person private personal data to harass, intimidate, or inflict harm is illegal.",
  "rulePrivacy04Penalty": "Maximum 5 years imprisonment and/or a maximum fine of Rp 5,000,000,000",
  "rulePrivacy04Explanation": "Disclosing identity numbers, phone contacts, residential addresses, or financial data on the internet with intent to intimidate or harm individuals constitutes criminal doxxing punishable by severe prison terms.",
  "rulePrivacy04Dos": "Redact and blur identity numbers, full names, and phone numbers when publishing transaction receipts\nReport malicious doxxing content to platform trust teams and law enforcement cyber units",
  "rulePrivacy04Donts": "Post identity cards of commercial counterparties online under pretext of debt collection\nCompile directories of personal citizen records without explicit written data consent",
  "rulePrivacy05Title": "Criminal Penalties for Online Fraud & Phishing",
  "rulePrivacy05Summary": "Disseminating fraudulent information in electronic transactions that causes consumer financial loss is a criminal offense.",
  "rulePrivacy05Penalty": "Maximum 6 years imprisonment and/or a maximum fine of Rp 1,000,000,000",
  "rulePrivacy05Explanation": "Intentionally distributing false or deceitful claims in digital commerce (bogus storefronts, APK phishing links, fraudulent investment traps) triggers statutory criminal prosecution under cyber laws.",
  "rulePrivacy05Dos": "Use verified marketplace escrow systems or authorized payment facilitators\nCheck recipient bank account legitimacy on the official government portal (cekrekening.id)",
  "rulePrivacy05Donts": "Download or open unverified .APK files sent via chat messaging apps\nTransfer money directly without escrow protection to unknown anonymous sellers",
  "ruleConsumer01Title": "Right to Compensation for Defective Goods",
  "ruleConsumer01Summary": "Consumers are legally entitled to compensation, reimbursement, or replacement for defective or damaged goods.",
  "ruleConsumer01Penalty": "Maximum 5 years imprisonment or a maximum fine of Rp 2,000,000,000",
  "ruleConsumer01Explanation": "Article 19 of the Consumer Protection Law requires business operators to indemnify consumers through refunds or equivalent replacements for damages, contamination, or harm caused by using defective products or services.",
  "ruleConsumer01Dos": "Record an unedited, continuous unboxing video from sealed package state\nKeep order invoices, digital receipts, and bank transaction slips handy",
  "ruleConsumer01Donts": "Accept parcels with torn or tampered safety seals without courier remarks\nDiscard physical purchase receipts before fully testing product operation",
  "ruleConsumer02Title": "Prohibition Against Unfair \"No Return\" Clauses",
  "ruleConsumer02Summary": "Standard contract clauses stating \"goods sold are non-refundable or non-exchangeable\" are void by law.",
  "ruleConsumer02Penalty": "Maximum 5 years imprisonment or a maximum fine of Rp 2,000,000,000",
  "ruleConsumer02Explanation": "Article 18 of the Consumer Protection Law prohibits standard clauses that unilaterally evade merchant liability, including blanket disclaimers rejecting returns when latent factory defects are present.",
  "ruleConsumer02Dos": "Assert exchange rights if products suffer hidden defects regardless of disclaimer text\nFile complaints against abusive clauses with the Consumer Dispute Settlement Agency (BPSK)",
  "ruleConsumer02Donts": "Surrender rights when merchants refuse returns solely citing receipt disclaimers\nDraft sales agreements that extinguish statutory consumer complaint rights",
  "ruleConsumer03Title": "Mandatory Indonesian Labeling & Expiry Dates",
  "ruleConsumer03Summary": "Circulating consumer goods must bear explicit local language labeling and clear expiration dates.",
  "ruleConsumer03Penalty": "Maximum 5 years imprisonment or a maximum fine of Rp 2,000,000,000",
  "ruleConsumer03Explanation": "Commercial operators are prohibited from trading goods lacking Indonesian instructional labels, official distribution permits (BPOM / SNI certificates), or readable expiry dates on product packaging.",
  "ruleConsumer03Dos": "Verify expiry dates and official food/drug authority (BPOM) registration codes before buying\nEnsure product packaging displays readable ingredient lists and safety warnings",
  "ruleConsumer03Donts": "Purchase imported cosmetics or pharmaceuticals lacking authorized distribution stamps\nResell or repurpose food inventory past official best-before or expiration dates",
  "ruleConsumer04Title": "Right to Truthful Information & Misleading Ads Ban",
  "ruleConsumer04Summary": "Businesses are strictly prohibited from advertising products with deceptive, untruthful, or exaggerated claims.",
  "ruleConsumer04Penalty": "Maximum 5 years imprisonment or a maximum fine of Rp 2,000,000,000",
  "ruleConsumer04Explanation": "Articles 9 and 10 of the Consumer Protection Law prohibit deceptive marketing claims, fictional discounts, or fabricated testimonials designed to mislead or deceive consumers.",
  "ruleConsumer04Dos": "Compare product price histories before major sales events to identify real discounts\nScrutinize instant miracle cure claims on over-the-counter dietary supplements",
  "ruleConsumer04Donts": "Manufacture fake sale discounts by inflating baseline prices right before promotions\nDeploy fabricated testimonials or paid influencer posts without explicit sponsored tags",
  "ruleSafety01Title": "Fire Extinguisher & Emergency Evacuation Requirements",
  "ruleSafety01Summary": "Public and commercial buildings must maintain inspected fire extinguishers and clear evacuation escape routes.",
  "ruleSafety01Penalty": "Written notices, suspension of building occupancy certificate (SLF), or complete closure",
  "ruleSafety01Explanation": "Occupational safety and building codes mandate that commercial buildings provide inspected, operational fire extinguishers every 15 meters, pressurized emergency stairwells, and evacuation doors that remain unlocked throughout working hours.",
  "ruleSafety01Dos": "Verify fire extinguisher pressure needles remain strictly within green indicator zones\nKeep emergency exit corridors and stairwells completely free of stored materials",
  "ruleSafety01Donts": "Padlock or chain emergency exit doors during business operations\nObstruct illuminated green EXIT signage with banners or marketing materials",
  "ruleSafety02Title": "Construction Safety Standards & Mandatory PPE",
  "ruleSafety02Summary": "Personnel and visitors within active construction zones must wear compliant Personal Protective Equipment (PPE).",
  "ruleSafety02Penalty": "Administrative fines, immediate work stoppage orders, or contractor license revocation",
  "ruleSafety02Explanation": "Statutory occupational safety laws require project employers to provide approved hard hats, steel-toe safety footwear, high-visibility vests, and certified full-body harnesses when performing work at elevations exceeding 1.8 meters.",
  "ruleSafety02Dos": "Hook double lanyards of your full-body harness securely to certified lifelines or scaffolds\nWear an approved hard hat with chinstraps fastened tightly inside work zones",
  "ruleSafety02Donts": "Enter active construction zones wearing open sandals, flip-flops, or casual shoes\nWork on elevated staging without perimeter toe-boards and fall guardrails",
  "ruleSafety03Title": "Smoke-Free Zone (KTR) Regulations",
  "ruleSafety03Summary": "Smoking and vaping are strictly prohibited in healthcare facilities, schools, places of worship, and transit.",
  "ruleSafety03Penalty": "Individual fines up to Rp 50,000,000 or up to 6 months imprisonment under municipal bylaws",
  "ruleSafety03Explanation": "National health legislation mandates building administrators enforce designated Smoke-Free Areas (KTR). Using tobacco cigarettes or electronic vape devices within restricted boundaries incurs municipal administrative and penal sanctions.",
  "ruleSafety03Dos": "Smoke exclusively within designated outdoor smoking zones situated away from building portals\nExtinguish cigarette butts completely in ash receptacles until free of glowing embers",
  "ruleSafety03Donts": "Puff cigarettes or vapes in hospital corridors, daycare classrooms, or elevators\nToss smoldering cigarette butts into dry foliage, grass, or combustible trash bins",
  "ruleSafety04Title": "Emergency Response & Right to Refuse Dangerous Work",
  "ruleSafety04Summary": "Workers have the absolute legal right to refuse tasks that pose imminent life-threatening hazards without protective gear.",
  "ruleSafety04Penalty": "Criminal confinement or financial penalties for employers coercing workers into imminent danger",
  "ruleSafety04Explanation": "Article 12 of the Occupational Safety Act legally protects a worker right to halt tasks and refuse work if mandatory health, safety controls, or personal protective equipment are missing, posing immediate risks to life or physical well-being.",
  "ruleSafety04Dos": "Formally report unsafe site conditions or dangerous practices to Safety Officers\nMemorize the precise location of designated outdoor Assembly Points at your facility",
  "ruleSafety04Donts": "Enter enclosed confined spaces lacking forced-air ventilation blowers and gas detectors\nPenalize or deduct wages of employees exercising lawful rights to refuse unshielded hazards",
  "ruleEthics01Title": "Ban on Gratuities & Bribery of Public Officials",
  "ruleEthics01Summary": "Gifts, hospitality, or favors conferred upon public servants are legally presumed bribes if connected to their official duties.",
  "ruleEthics01Penalty": "Life imprisonment or 4 to 20 years prison plus fines up to Rp 1,000,000,000",
  "ruleEthics01Explanation": "Article 12B of the Anti-Corruption Law presumes any gratuity given to a civil servant or public official constitutes illegal bribery unless formally reported to the Corruption Eradication Commission (KPK) within 30 working days.",
  "ruleEthics01Dos": "Report any official holiday hampers or vendor gifts to internal Anti-Gratuity Units or KPK\nDecline cash envelopes and luxury hospitality offered by prospective procurement vendors",
  "ruleEthics01Donts": "Gift expensive festive hampers or electronics to government contract commitment officers\nOffer facilitation money at public permit service desks to expedite processing queues",
  "ruleEthics02Title": "Whistleblower & Witness Protection Rights",
  "ruleEthics02Summary": "Whistleblowers reporting corruption or organized crime are guaranteed identity confidentiality and statutory immunity.",
  "ruleEthics02Penalty": "Up to 7 years imprisonment for individuals retaliating against or intimidating protected witnesses",
  "ruleEthics02Explanation": "The Witness and Victim Protection Act guarantees bona fide whistleblowers cannot be prosecuted civilly or criminally for truthful reports, and authorizes physical security and procedural accommodations via the LPSK agency.",
  "ruleEthics02Dos": "Compile evidentiary records, audit trails, and receipts prior to filing with LPSK or KPK\nUtilize secure, encrypted internal Whistleblowing Systems (WBS) to safeguard anonymity",
  "ruleEthics02Donts": "Disclose real whistleblower identities to workplace colleagues or public social channels\nDemote, reassign, or dismiss employees for reporting corporate malfeasance in good faith",
  "ruleEthics03Title": "Conflict of Interest Ban in Procurement Activities",
  "ruleEthics03Summary": "Procurement officials are prohibited from involving family-held or personal enterprises in government tenders.",
  "ruleEthics03Penalty": "Contract annulment, commercial blacklisting, and prosecution under Article 12i of Anti-Corruption Law",
  "ruleEthics03Explanation": "Article 12i of the Anti-Corruption Act strictly forbids public officers from participating directly or indirectly in tenders, contracts, or concessions that they are assigned to manage, review, or supervise.",
  "ruleEthics03Dos": "Sign and submit formal Conflict of Interest declarations before procurement panels convene\nRecuse yourself from tender evaluations when any bidding firm employs family relations",
  "ruleEthics03Donts": "Award contracts to preferred insider entities bypassing technical appraisal and competitive bidding\nSplit procurement value packages artificially to evade mandatory open electronic tender auctions",
  "ruleEthics04Title": "Medical Confidentiality & Doctor-Patient Relationship",
  "ruleEthics04Summary": "Healthcare professionals are legally bound to protect the strict confidentiality of patient clinical records.",
  "ruleEthics04Penalty": "Ethical disciplinary actions, practice license revocations (SIP), and criminal breach of privacy prosecution",
  "ruleEthics04Explanation": "Health statutes and medical record regulations dictate that clinical records remain strictly confidential property of the patient. Disclosure of medical files without express written patient consent is only permissible under valid judicial court orders.",
  "ruleEthics04Dos": "Secure verified written informed consent prior to administering any invasive clinical procedure\nStore physical medical records in secured vaults and safeguard electronic health charts with encryption",
  "ruleEthics04Donts": "Discuss patient clinical histories or post wound treatment photography on personal social profiles\nRelease patient summaries or test diagnostics to insurance representatives without signed patient authorization",
